    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2FTDGqZrVLEEXS9bCedsnWx)_\n\nFollow-up to #300.\n\n## What\n- Registry check: `sp-notes-filing-lint` first compares the tags of `sp-notes-filing-rules` with the tag registry and asks (`y-or-n-p`) to register each missing one via `sp-org-tag-add`. A refused tag is reported and the lint still runs.\n- `sp-notes-filing` (module, doc, tests) is folded into `sp-notes` (`libraries/modules/academic/sp-notes.el`, doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-notes.org`). The doc and commentary point to `sp-litnotes`, which writes into the `litnotes/` folder that the `litnote` rule uses.\n- New [ADR 0024](adr/0024-remove-denote-file-notes-by-tag.org) records the decision to remove Denote and file notes by tag; ADR 0010 is marked superseded.\n- Tests moved to `tests/sp-notes-test.el` (11 pass in batch Emacs 29).\n\nNot run on the real vault.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCLuV4PSf39usC3bgD)_",
